{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>YHWH goes forth like a warrior.</b> An allusion to the decrees that go forth by the name HaShem, which were in secret." "<b>He is zealous.</b> On account of the Babylonians, servants of Bel." "<b>He will shout.</b> From תרועה." "<b>He will roar.</b> Like מר צורח (Zephaniah 1:14), 'he will cry out.' And if they are two, [it is] binyan." "<b>He will prevail.</b> That He defeats Babylon."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:35.693584862Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}